==================================================================================================
0. HOW TO READ THIS FILE
==================================================================================================

NOTATION   This file uses a local, self-describing declarative notation chosen by Artifact 067.
           It is an implementation choice, not COOLBOY12 architecture, and establishes no
           repository-wide schema language (SC-067-D). No parser exists for it.

           ELEMENT <name>        a structural element of a materialized Record
           LAYER                 ENVELOPE (universal, RMS §4) or FAMILY (Registry-model-owned)
           REQUIRED              yes | no
           CARDINALITY           exactly-one | …
           CONSTRAINT            what a conforming value must satisfy
           BASIS                 SOURCE FACT · REQUIRED SYNTHESIS · 067 CHOICE, with its source
           REJECT                a value that does not conform

STATUS     This contract describes the structure a materialized MODEL-DEFINITION Record must
           satisfy. It is not a MODEL-DEFINITION Record, not a SCHEMA-DEFINITION Record, and not
           canonical data. It is an authored source outside canon/** (Roadmap §0.8; CONFLICT-F).
           Concrete MODEL-DEFINITION Records are committed only through the Mutation
           Coordinator (row 152) after G-CANON-R. Where this contract differs from the Master
           Blueprint, the Record Model System, the Roadmap, or Artifact 066, those sources are
           right and this contract is wrong.

SPEC       Artifact 066 — docs/registry/model_definition.md — is the semantic contract this file
           encodes. It is consumed unchanged.

==================================================================================================
1. RECORD SHAPE
==================================================================================================

MODEL-DEFINITION RECORD
├── ENVELOPE  partition · kind · object_id · slug · provenance · registry_ref · sot_class
└── FAMILY    model_subject · definition

Exactly these nine elements. The envelope is the universal seven (RMS §4); the family has two.
No other element is part of this contract.

==================================================================================================
2. ENVELOPE — the universal seven (RMS §4; Artifact 033)
==================================================================================================

Types, defaults, nullability and serialization of the envelope fields are not established by
the governing sources (Artifact 033) and are not stated here.

ELEMENT     partition
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  R — the Registry partition
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — a MODEL-DEFINITION is a Registry Record (RMS §10, §10.1; 066 §5)

ELEMENT     kind
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  identifies the declared Registry Kind MODEL-DEFINITION (Kind 1 of RMS §10.1)
            The constraint is symbolic. No two-character Registry Kind code is established;
            none is minted here (SC-067-E).
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §10.1; Artifact 064 §8. The code is Registry content bound later
            (row 117; Artifact 060 writes it schematically as <kind>).
REJECT      any other Registry Kind; any invented code (for example MD) presented as established

ELEMENT     object_id
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the object identity component under the universal identity grammar
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4, §5; 066 RS-1

ELEMENT     slug
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  decoration only; never identity, never the basis of resolution
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §5; Artifact 033

ELEMENT     provenance
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  as the universal envelope carries it; provenance meaning is not defined here
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4; Artifact 033

ELEMENT     registry_ref
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the universal envelope field, unchanged. This contract attaches no referent,
            self-reference convention, bootstrap target or resolution meaning to it.
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4; Artifact 033 leaves its referent unresolved; Blueprint §9.4:
            reference resolution is not Registry work

ELEMENT     sot_class
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  as the universal envelope carries it. No value is fixed here; Artifact 067's own
            manifest SoT and Canon are not Record-level values and are not copied into it.
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4; Artifact 033

==================================================================================================
3. FAMILY — MODEL-DEFINITION content (Registry-model-owned; not envelope fields)
==================================================================================================

ELEMENT     model_subject
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  one value from the closed set   W | E | P | R | V | I
              W  World       E  Epistemic   P  Production
              R  Registry    V  Visual      I  Issue
            The value names a declared sovereign Record Model itself — a declaration-level
            subject — never a Record of that model.
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 066 MD-1 (one declared model subject), MD-2 (declared first),
            §9 (the six, and only the six); RMS §2; Artifact 063 §8.2 (declared Record Model as
            an admissible target). The element NAME is a 067 CHOICE.
REJECT      no value                                      (MD-1)
            two or more values, e.g. W and E together     (MD-1)
            any value outside the set, e.g. S "Simulation" claimed as a seventh model
                                                          (RMS §2; 066 MD-7)
            a Record identifier, e.g. W-CH-…-Maximus      (domain instance; RMS §10.3; RF-4)
            a runtime object or service                   (RMS §10.3; RF-5)

ELEMENT     definition
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the governed model-level meaning of the declared model named by model_subject.
            Non-empty. Its internal form is not prescribed by this contract.
            It may state the model's source-established question (RMS §6); it is not required
            to. It does not supply, override or standardize the model's Kind taxonomy, identity
            semantics, lifecycle, relationship packaging, temporal architecture, provenance
            meaning, canonicality meaning, semantic validation or package composition.
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 066 §5 (a definition carries governed meaning), MD-3
            (governs; never instantiates), MD-8 (model-owned semantics stay with the model);
            RMS §6.1. The element NAME, the single carrier and the non-empty rule are 067
            CHOICES.
REJECT      executable behaviour, a model factory, a registration or creation action
            (MD-3)
            a domain instance or runtime object used as the source of meaning (RF-4, RF-5)

==================================================================================================
4. STRUCTURAL PROHIBITIONS
==================================================================================================

P-01  No element beyond the nine of §1. In particular none of: version, revision, latest,
      supersedes, deprecated, replacement, effective_at, compatibility, status, tier,
      lifecycle_state, canonical, history, relationship_record, owner, owns_records,
      grants_sovereignty, authority_over_model, implementation, service, worker, session,
      process, handler, factory.
P-02  No generic reference list (definition_refs, kind_refs, schema_refs, contract_refs,
      dependencies, related_records). Admissible target categories are not concrete relations;
      the only concrete relation is the declared model subject (066 RF-3; Artifact 063 RB-5).
P-03  No element names, carries or implies ownership of the defined model or of its Records, or
      grants sovereignty. W, E, P, V and I keep their Records; Registry owns R Records by its
      own sovereignty, not by a MODEL-DEFINITION (066 MD-4).
P-04  No inheritance, parent model, template model or shared interior among W, E, P, R, V, I
      (RMS §2; 066 MD-5).
P-05  No envelope field added, removed or renamed; the family elements are not envelope
      fields (RMS §4).
P-06  None of RMS §4's prohibited universal semantics: Record base, Relationship Record,
      History Record, lifecycle, canonicality, Kind taxonomy, identity composition, state
      model, semantic schema.
P-07  Not a KIND-DEFINITION, SCHEMA-DEFINITION or SIMULATION-MODEL-DEFINITION contract
      (066 MD-6, MD-7).

==================================================================================================
5. BOUNDARIES
==================================================================================================

RESOLUTION      A conforming Record is identity-bearing (§2), so the shared resolution mechanism
                can resolve it once committed. This contract implements no resolver, lookup,
                index or storage. Resolution never relies on slug or on model_subject.
                Resolvable is not legal (Artifact 063 §11). Registry definition resolution by
                id+version is row 115's; create/resolve/version operations are row 114's.
                (066 RS-1 to RS-5)

VERSIONABILITY  Nothing here prevents the Registry evolution and versioning model of rows
                108–110 from applying to a MODEL-DEFINITION. No version element, numbering,
                pinning, supersession, deprecation or retention is defined. (066 §11)

REFERENCES      The model subject is a declaration reference to a declared Record Model, not an
                R→R reference to a MODEL-DEFINITION Record (Artifact 063 §8.2; 066 RF-2). No
                W/E/P/V/I domain instance and no runtime instance is a target or an authority.
                A reference transfers no ownership or authority. (066 RF-1 to RF-7)

MATERIALIZATION This file is an authored source. A MODEL-DEFINITION Record conforming to it is
                committed to canon/registry/** only through the Mutation Coordinator after
                G-CANON-R (Roadmap §0.8, PART X). No Roadmap row currently names the artifact
                that commits the six MODEL-DEFINITION Records; that gap is recorded in CONFLICT-F
                and is not filled here.

==================================================================================================
6. DECISION CASES (schematic — no identifier is minted; nothing here is Registry data)
==================================================================================================

ACCEPT  model_subject W, definition carrying governed meaning about the World model — World is
        not created and no World Record is owned
ACCEPT  model_subject R — not a bootstrap mechanism (RMS §10.4); Registry already owns its R
        Records as the sovereign R model
ACCEPT  one Record each with model_subject W, E, P, R, V, I — the same contract, no shared model
        interior
REJECT  model_subject S, claimed as a seventh sovereign Record Model
REJECT  model_subject W-CH-…-Maximus — a World domain instance
REJECT  model_subject W and E together
REJECT  model_subject absent
REJECT  definition that depends on a running service to establish what the model means
REJECT  kind given as an invented code such as MD

